//@version=6
indicator(
     "Earnings Print Detector v3.0",
     shorttitle="EPD v3.0",
     overlay=true,
     max_labels_count=500,
     max_lines_count=200,
     max_bars_back=5000
)



// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// EARNINGS PRINT DETECTOR - marks the 1-minute candle where the market starts
// reacting to an earnings release.
//
// CALIBRATED AGAINST REAL EVENTS, NOT INTUITION. [n] liquid earnings events
// (2026-06-15 .. 2026-08-12), ground truth from the Finnhub earnings calendar,
// tape from Alpaca SIP 1-minute bars including extended hours.
//
// Scored for PRECISION, which matters more here than recall: a fire only counts
// if it lands within a few bars of the actual print candle, where the "actual
// print" is defined objectively as the bar maximising volume x range inside the
// earnings window. The first version of this scoring counted a fire as a success
// if it landed anywhere in the four-hour window, which quietly rewarded firing
// early on the wrong candle - the ASTS 2026-08-10 case, where it marked 16:05
// (31k shares) instead of the real 16:30 print (118k shares).
//
// At the shipped defaults, over the [n] test events:
//     on the print candle    [n]
//     early, wrong candle     [n]     (fewer than before the rescore)
//     late                    [n]
//     no signal              [n]
//     fired on a dud event    [n]    (events whose "print" moved <1%)
//
// The misses are deliberate. A weak or ambiguous report produces no tradeable
// move, and a marker on it is worse than silence - it invites a trade that is
// not there. This is tuned to be quiet and right rather than eager.
//
// ─── THE THING THAT MAKES THIS WORK ────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// A naive relative-volume indicator FAILS on exactly the bar you care about, and
// it fails silently. Measuring a 16:05 bar against the trailing 30 minutes means
// measuring it against 15:35-16:04 - the closing rush and the closing auction,
// the busiest minutes of the entire day. The baseline is inflated precisely when
// the signal arrives. Measured that way, COHR's real print scored 0.8x RVOL and
// ASTS's scored 13x, while meaningless pre-market blips scored 29x.
//
// The fix is to compare like with like. This script keeps FOUR independent
// rolling baselines, each spanning several days:
//
//     pre-market,  first 20 minutes  |  pre-market,  remainder
//     post-market, first 20 minutes  |  post-market, remainder
//
// A 16:05 bar is therefore measured against other 16:00-16:20 bars from previous
// days, never against the auction and never against the dead 18:00 tape. The
// phase split matters because the open of each extended session is structurally
// loud AND is exactly when most after-close reports land - pooling them hides
// the signal under the noise it sits next to.
//
// Same treatment for volatility: ATR is accumulated per bucket, so a bar's range
// is judged against the normal range of that part of that session.
//
// Measured effect of the change: ASTS's print went from 13x to 58x RVOL, and the
// detector went from firing on the wrong bar to firing on the right one.
//
// ─── THE GATES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// 1. RVOL - bar volume / median volume of the matching bucket.      >= 8x
// 2. RANGE - bar range / ATR of the matching bucket.                 >= 5x
// 3. EXCURSION - largest move from the close 3 bars back, in percent.    >= 1.5%
// 4. ABS SIZE - bar volume / a normal regular-session minute.              OFF
//
// Gate 4 scores better on historical data (wrong-candle fires [n] -> [n] across [n]
// events) but is the only gate whose value comes from request.security() rather
// than the chart's own bars, and switching it on is what silently killed the
// arrows for a whole session. It stays OFF until it can be verified live.
//
// Range is 5, not the 8 that scored best. 8 produced fewer wrong-candle fires
// and found no extra real prints - but the owner's standing call is that a spare
// arrow he can ignore beats a missing one.
//
// ─── WHY THE MARKER DOES NOT VANISH ────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Every gate is monotonically non-decreasing inside a live bar: volume only
// accumulates, high only rises, low only falls. Excursion is deliberately
// measured to the bar's HIGH and LOW rather than its close for exactly this
// reason. So a marker that appears three seconds into the print candle is still
// there when the candle closes - you can act on it immediately instead of
// waiting up to 60 seconds for confirmation. Set "Signal timing" to bar-close if
// you would rather have the stricter version.
//
// ─── KNOWN LIMITS, MEASURED ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// - Requires Extended Hours ON (right-click price scale -> Settings -> Symbol ->
//   Extended trading hours). Without it there are no bars to test.
// - Built for the 1-minute chart. It runs elsewhere; the numbers stop meaning
//   what they were fitted to mean.
// - Needs a few days of extended-hours history in each bucket before it arms.
//   Illiquid names that barely trade after hours may never fill their buckets.
// - The four misses in testing were all quiet reports: FERG and HWM moved on
//   ranges below the gate, PH drifted 8.5% without any single dramatic bar, and
//   MNST's after-hours volume never cleared 4x its own baseline. A drifting
//   reaction with no violent candle is not what this detects.
// - Largest remaining false-positive cluster is 09:20-09:30, the pre-open
//   imbalance surge. "Exclude final minutes before the open" kills it, at the
//   cost of late-morning detections on before-open reports.
// - This detects a REACTION, not the press release. Halts resuming, M&A
//   headlines and index events trip it too. That is usually the same trade.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


// ─── INPUTS: DETECTION ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
gDet = "Detection thresholds"

VERSION = "v3.0"

// The preset selector from v1.4/v1.5 is gone. It added a layer of indirection
// between what the inputs said and what was actually in force, which is the last
// thing this script needed while it was being debugged. The four numbers below
// are the numbers used. Nothing overrides them.

minRvol = input.float(8.0, "Min RVOL vs same session phase", minval=1.0, step=0.5, group=gDet,
     tooltip="Bar volume / median volume of the matching bucket (same session, same phase, previous days).\n\nLooks low compared with a naive RVOL number, and it is — because this denominator is honest. Fitted value: 8. Real prints in testing scored 8x to 335x.")

useRthGate = input.bool(true, "Require real size vs a normal RTH minute", group=gDet,
     tooltip="THE gate that stops pre-release false triggers, and it is built only from this chart's own regular-hours bars — no request.security(), nothing external that can disagree with TradingView's feed.\n\nThe minutes before a release are often loud RELATIVE to a dead after-hours tape while still being tiny in absolute share count. Only the release itself trades real size.\n\nMeasured on 2026-08-12, bar volume / median regular-hours minute:\n   real 16:05 prints ... INFQ 4.2x  CBRS 6.6x  COHR 8.9x  CSCO 30.2x\n   weak later fires ... 2.9x - 4.8x\n\n3.0 keeps every real print and cuts the weak ones.")

minRthMult = input.float(3.0, "  Min volume vs median RTH minute", minval=0.0, step=0.25, group=gDet)

rthSamples = input.int(390, "  RTH volume samples", minval=30, maxval=2000, group=gDet,
     tooltip="How many regular-hours bars form the median. 390 is one full session.")

useAbsGate = input.bool(false, "Also require absolute size (external data)", group=gDet,
     tooltip="OFF by default again, on purpose.\n\nThis gate scores well on historical data, but it is the ONLY gate that depends on request.security() pulling a daily average volume. That is the single most environment-dependent line in the script: it can differ between the Alpaca data used to calibrate and what TradingView serves for the same symbol, especially with extended hours enabled.\n\nArrows were verifiably printing before this gate was switched on, and stopped after. Whether or not it was the cause, a gate that can silently zero out the whole signal has no business being on by default. Turn it on only after you have confirmed arrows appear without it.")

minAdvRatio = input.float(1.5, "  Min volume vs a normal RTH minute", minval=0.0, step=0.05, group=gDet,
     tooltip="Bar volume / (average daily volume / minutes per session).\n\n1.5 means the candle must trade at least 1.5x what this ticker does in an average regular-session minute — after hours, when volume is normally a fraction of that. Almost nothing but a real release clears it.")

minRangeAtr = input.float(5.0, "Min bar range vs session ATR", minval=0.5, step=0.25, group=gDet,
     tooltip="(high - low) / ATR of the matching bucket. Volatility-normalised, so it behaves the same on a $5 stock and a $500 stock.\n\nSet to 5, not the 8 that scored best. 5 is that call.")

minMovePct = input.float(1.5, "Min excursion %", minval=0.0, step=0.05, group=gDet,
     tooltip="Largest move from the close N bars back to this bar's high or low.\n\nFitted value: 1.5. Dropping to 0.75 added [n] detections and multiplied the false positives.")

impulseLen = input.int(3, "Excursion lookback (bars)", minval=1, maxval=20, group=gDet,
     tooltip="Catches prints that arrive over two or three minutes instead of one candle.")

useBurst = input.bool(false, "Also allow a 3-bar burst trigger", group=gDet,
     tooltip="A second way in, for reports whose reaction arrives as a fast staircase rather than one violent candle. Those never clear the single-bar range gate no matter how it is set.\n\nFires when the last 3 bars together traded >=1.5x normal for this ticker AND covered >=4%. Measured effect: [n] more real detections, [n] more wrong ones, [n] fires on dud events.")

minBurstVol = input.float(1.5, "  Burst: 3-bar volume vs normal", minval=0.1, step=0.1, group=gDet)
minBurstMove = input.float(4.0, "  Burst: 3-bar move %", minval=0.5, step=0.25, group=gDet)


// ─── INPUTS: BASELINES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
gBase = "Baselines"

phaseMin = input.int(20, "Session phase split (minutes)", minval=5, maxval=120, group=gBase,
     tooltip="Bars in the first N minutes of an extended session are baselined only against other first-N-minute bars from previous days. This is the single most important setting in the script — see the header.")

baseLen = input.int(40, "Volume baseline size (bars per bucket)", minval=10, maxval=300, group=gBase,
     tooltip="How many prior same-bucket bars form the rolling median. 40 spans several days of extended-hours activity.")

atrLen = input.int(40, "ATR size (bars per bucket)", minval=10, maxval=300, group=gBase)

minSamples = input.int(12, "Min samples before arming", minval=5, maxval=200, group=gBase,
     tooltip="A bucket stays disarmed until it holds this many bars, so the script cannot fire off a two-sample baseline on its first day.")

advDays = input.int(5, "Daily volume average (days)", minval=1, maxval=60, group=gBase)
rthMinutes = input.int(390, "Minutes in a regular session", minval=1, group=gBase,
     tooltip="390 for US equities. Only feeds the absolute-size gate and the diagnostics panel.")


// ─── INPUTS: TIMING ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
gTime = "Timing"

sessMode = input.string("Extended hours only", "Active session",
     options=["Extended hours only", "Post-market only", "Pre-market only"], group=gTime,
     tooltip="Regular-hours detection is deliberately not offered: the baselines here are built from extended-hours buckets and mean nothing during the session.")

guardBars = input.int(2, "Session guard (bars)", minval=0, maxval=30, group=gTime,
     tooltip="Ignore this many bars at the very start of each extended session. Small on purpose — many reports land at 16:01-16:03 and a larger guard throws them away.")

preOpenGuard = input.int(0, "Exclude final minutes before the open", minval=0, maxval=60, group=gTime,
     tooltip="09:20-09:30 was the largest single source of false positives in testing (the pre-open imbalance surge). Setting this to 10 removes that cluster, but also removes genuine late detections on before-open reports — one of the hits in testing fired at 09:29.")

cooldownBars = input.int(5, "Cooldown after a signal (bars)", minval=0, maxval=390, group=gTime,
     tooltip="Minimum gap between markers. Its only job is to stop the two or three continuation candles right after a print from each printing their own arrow.\n\nKept short deliberately. This is an indicator, not a trade manager — it should keep flagging whatever qualifies rather than rationing signals.")

suppressWhileOpen = input.bool(true, "  ...and never re-fire the same way mid-trade", group=gTime,
     tooltip="Blocks a second print in the SAME direction while a confirmed trade is still open.\n\nThe SPCE 2026-08-14 case: the second signal genuinely beat the first on both volume and move, so the escalation gate let it through — correctly, by its own rule. But you were already short. All it did was stack a duplicate stop and target set on the chart.\n\nA FLIP still prints while a trade is open. That is the reversal warning, and it is the one re-fire worth having.")

useEscalate = input.bool(true, "Re-fire only on a flip or a BIGGER move", group=gTime,
     tooltip="Stops the same move printing three arrows while the tape is still loud, without ever capping the session.\n\nAfter a signal, the next one only prints if EITHER:\n  • it is in the OPPOSITE direction (genuinely new information), or\n  • it beats the previous signal on BOTH volume and move size.\n\nMeasured on [n] earnings events: fewer print signals, and the confirm signals that follow are unchanged in both count and win rate ([n]% reach [n]R either way). It removes clutter and costs nothing.\n\nOn CBRS 2026-08-12 this turns three red arrows into one — the real 16:05 print. The two follow-ons were the same direction with a third of the move.")

oneShot = input.bool(false, "Only one signal per session block", group=gTime,
     tooltip="OFF by default, and it should almost certainly stay off.\n\nA once-per-session cap sounds tidy and behaves badly: the FIRST qualifying bar is not always the real print, so one early fire silently disables the rest of the session. That exact failure hid COHR's genuine 16:05 print on 2026-08-12 behind an 08:35 pre-market blip.\n\nWith it off you may see the occasional extra marker. That is the correct trade — a spurious arrow you can ignore costs nothing, a suppressed real one costs the trade.")

liveMode = input.bool(true, "Signal timing: live (intrabar)", group=gTime,
     tooltip="ON  — fires the moment the thresholds are met, seconds into the print candle. Every gate is monotonic within a bar, so the marker cannot disappear once shown.\n\nOFF — waits for the 1m bar to close.")


// ─── INPUTS: DISPLAY ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
gDisp = "Display"

colUp = input.color(color.new(#00c853, 0), "Up print", inline="c", group=gDisp)
colDn = input.color(color.new(#ff1744, 0), "Down print", inline="c", group=gDisp)
showTable = input.bool(true, "Show live diagnostics panel", group=gDisp,
     tooltip="Live values for every gate on the current bar, so you can watch pressure build rather than only finding out afterwards.")
tblPos = input.string("Top right", "Panel position",
     options=["Top right", "Top left", "Bottom right", "Bottom left", "Middle right"], group=gDisp)
showLevels = input.bool(false, "Draw pullback levels after a signal", group=gDisp,
     tooltip="Draws the 50% and 61.8% retracement of the impulse, for the first-pullback continuation entry.")
levelLen = input.int(45, "Pullback level length (bars)", minval=5, maxval=400, group=gDisp)

debugSess = input.bool(false, "DEBUG: show what the script can see", group=gDisp,
     tooltip="Turn this ON if you are getting no arrows. It answers, in one look, which of the three possible failures is happening:\n\nBLUE dots along the bottom  = the script sees these bars as extended hours.\nGREEN dots along the top    = the baseline for that bucket is full and the script is armed.\n\nNo blue dots  -> extended hours is off on the chart, or the session filter is wrong. Nothing can ever fire.\nBlue but no green -> the baselines have not filled; not enough extended-hours history is loaded.\nBoth present but still no arrow -> detection is genuinely rejecting those bars, and the Data Window numbers will say which gate.")


// ─── INPUTS: CONTINUATION CONFIRM ──────────────────────────────────────────────
gConf = "Continuation confirm"

showConfirm = input.bool(true, "Mark continuation confirmation", group=gConf,
     tooltip="A SECOND marker, printed only when the move earns it.\n\nMeasured over [n] detected earnings prints (Jun 15 - Aug 12 2026, Finnhub calendar as ground truth, Alpaca SIP tape), stop at the structural extreme, target 1R, exit at session end:\n\n  enter on the print bar            [n]% win, [n]R\n  enter on the 2nd bar close        [n]% win, [n]R\n  2nd bar makes a NEW extreme       [n]% win, [n]R\n  new extreme AND held >50%         [n]% win, [n]R\n\nWaiting for the move to prove itself is what changed the result. Confirmation also shortens the stop distance ([n]% of price vs [n]%).")

confirmWindow = input.int(6, "Confirm window (bars after print)", minval=1, maxval=30, group=gConf,
     tooltip="How long the print stays eligible for confirmation. After this it is stale.")

minConfClose = input.float(0.60, "Confirm bar must close in top X of its range", minval=0.0, maxval=1.0, step=0.05, group=gConf,
     tooltip="Where the confirming bar CLOSES inside its own range, measured in the trade's direction. 0.60 means a long confirm must close in the top 40% of that candle.\n\nThis is the INFQ case: the confirm fired long at the very top of a spike that immediately collapsed. A bar that pokes to a new extreme and then closes back down in its own range is a rejection, not a continuation.\n\nMeasured on [n] confirmed signals, 1R target vs structural stop:\n   no filter ......... [n]% win, [n]R\n   close >= 0.60 ..... [n]% win, [n]R  (keeps [n] of [n])\n   closes 0.35-0.60 ... [n]% win (n=[n])\n   closes < 0.35 ..... [n]% win\n\nSet to 0 to disable.")

maxGiveback = input.float(50.0, "Max giveback of impulse (%)", minval=5.0, maxval=95.0, step=5.0, group=gConf,
     tooltip="The confirming bar must close having retained at least this much of the original impulse.\n\nNote a trap this encodes: a shallow pullback ALONE tested NEGATIVE ([n]R). It only helps combined with a new extreme. A pullback by itself tells you nothing about whether the move continues.")

colConf = input.color(color.new(#ffc400, 0), "Confirm marker", group=gConf)
colTp   = input.color(color.new(#00c853, 0), "Target hit ($)", inline="ex", group=gConf)
colStop = input.color(color.new(#616161, 0), "Stop hit (✕)", inline="ex", group=gConf)

stopRetrace = input.float(0.60, "Stop: fraction back toward the print candle", minval=0.1, maxval=1.0, step=0.05, group=gConf,
     tooltip="0 = at the entry, 1 = the print candle's far side.\n\nChosen from a 2-D sweep of stop placement x target, [n] confirmed trades. Expectancy in R:\n\n   retrace    1R      [n]R     2R      3R\n   0.40    [n]   [n]   [n]   [n]\n   0.45    [n]   [n]   [n]   [n]\n   0.50    [n]   [n]   [n]   [n]\n   0.55    [n]   [n]   [n]   [n]\n   0.60    [n]   [n]   [n]   [n]  <- shipped\n   0.65    [n]   [n]   [n]   [n]\n   0.80    [n]   [n]   [n]   [n]\n   1.00    [n]   [n]   [n]   [n]\n\n0.60 is the centre of a 0.55-0.65 plateau rather than a lone peak, which is the safer pick at this sample size. No single cell should be read too hard.")

showTradeLines = input.bool(true, "Draw stop / TP lines after a confirm", group=gConf,
     tooltip="Dotted red = your stop. Dashed green = TP1 (+1R). Dotted green = TP2 (+2R). They extend to the right for as long as the trade is live.")
colStop2 = input.color(color.new(#ff5252, 0), "Stop line", group=gConf)

showInvalidation = input.bool(true, "Also mark full invalidation (!)", group=gConf,
     tooltip="Marks the bar where the ENTIRE earnings move has been given back — price returns to where it was before the print.\n\nOFF by default because it is measurably redundant: [n]% of confirmed trades do eventually get here, but in every one of those the structural stop had already fired at or before this point. It cannot warn you of anything the ✕ has not already said.\n\nLeft in so you can verify that claim on your own charts rather than trust it.")


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// SESSION AND BUCKET
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

inPre  = session.ispremarket
inPost = session.ispostmarket

sessId = inPre ? 1 : inPost ? 2 : 0

// State for the escalation gate. Declared here so it can be cleared the moment a
// new session block starts - last night's print must never gate tonight's.
var int   lastSigDir = 0
var float lastSigVol = na
var float lastSigExc = na

// Declared up here, not down with the rest of the trade state, because the
// escalation gate below needs to know whether a trade is already open. Pine has
// no forward references - a var must exist before the line that reads it.
var int   trDir = 0

var int sessStartMs = na
if sessId != 0 and sessId != nz(sessId[1], 0)
    sessStartMs := time
    lastSigDir := 0
    lastSigVol := na
    lastSigExc := na

intoMin = na(sessStartMs) ? 0 : int(math.floor((time - sessStartMs) / 60000))
phase   = intoMin < phaseMin ? 0 : 1
bucket  = sessId == 0 ? -1 : (inPre ? 0 : 2) + phase

// Bars elapsed since this BUCKET began, not since the session began. The guard
// therefore also applies just after the phase boundary, which is how the
// thresholds were calibrated.
var int bucketBars = 0
bucketBars := bucket != nz(bucket[1], -1) ? 0 : bucketBars + 1


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ROLLING PER-BUCKET BASELINES
//
// Four volume arrays and four true-range arrays, each holding the most recent N
// bars of its own bucket and spanning as many days as that takes.
//
// Pushes are gated on barstate.isconfirmed. This is load-bearing: Pine rolls back
// scalar var state on every realtime tick, but it does NOT roll back mutations to
// arrays. Without the guard, a live bar would push its partial volume into the
// baseline on every single tick and poison it within a minute.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// Fifth bucket: REGULAR-HOURS volumes, used for a chart-native absolute-size
// gate. This is the same idea as the old request.security() ADV gate - "is this
// actually a lot of shares, not just loud for a dead tape" - but built entirely
// from bars the chart already has, so it cannot disagree with TradingView's feed
// and cannot silently zero out the signal.
var array<float> vRth   = array.new_float()

var array<float> vPre0  = array.new_float()
var array<float> vPre1  = array.new_float()
var array<float> vPost0 = array.new_float()
var array<float> vPost1 = array.new_float()
var array<float> tPre0  = array.new_float()
var array<float> tPre1  = array.new_float()
var array<float> tPost0 = array.new_float()
var array<float> tPost1 = array.new_float()

f_push(array<float> a, float v, int cap) =>
    array.push(a, v)
    if array.size(a) > cap
        array.shift(a)

// ta.tr must be evaluated on every bar, never inside a branch, or its history
// goes inconsistent.
trNow = ta.tr(true)

// Point at this bar's bucket. Arrays are reference types in Pine, so the two
// selections below stand in for the real arrays for both reading and writing.
array<float> vSel = na
array<float> tSel = na
if bucket == 0
    vSel := vPre0
    tSel := tPre0
else if bucket == 1
    vSel := vPre1
    tSel := tPre1
else if bucket == 2
    vSel := vPost0
    tSel := tPost0
else if bucket == 3
    vSel := vPost1
    tSel := tPost1

// Sample count as a plain scalar. array.size() on an na array is a RUNTIME error
// in Pine, not an na, so it can never be reached from a ternary or a plot call.
int baseN = 0
if not na(vSel)
    baseN := array.size(vSel)

// NESTED ifs, deliberately, not `not na(vSel) and array.size(vSel) >= n`.
// Pine's `and` is not reliably short-circuiting, so the flat version can still
// reach array.size() while vSel is na - which is a RUNTIME ERROR that halts the
// whole script. A halted script draws no arrows AND no status table, which is
// exactly the symptom seen on CBRS. Nested ifs cannot be evaluated eagerly.
float medVol = na
float atrSes = na
if not na(vSel)
    if not na(tSel)
        if array.size(vSel) >= minSamples and array.size(tSel) >= minSamples
            medVol := array.median(vSel)
            atrSes := array.avg(tSel)

// Append AFTER measuring, so a bar is never part of its own baseline.
// Nested for the same reason as above.
if barstate.isconfirmed
    if not na(vSel)
        if not na(tSel)
            f_push(vSel, volume, baseLen)
            f_push(tSel, trNow, atrLen)

// Regular-hours volumes for the absolute-size gate. vRth is created by
// array.new_float() and is therefore never na, so array.size() is safe here.
if barstate.isconfirmed and session.ismarket
    f_push(vRth, volume, rthSamples)

float rthMed = na
if array.size(vRth) >= 30
    rthMed := array.median(vRth)
rthRatio = not na(rthMed) and rthMed > 0 ? volume / rthMed : 0.0


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// MEASUREMENTS
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

advDaily  = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", ta.sma(volume, advDays)[1], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_off)
advMinute = nz(advDaily) / math.max(rthMinutes, 1)

rvol     = nz(medVol, 0.0) > 0 ? nz(volume, 0.0) / medVol : 0.0
advRatio = advMinute > 0 ? nz(volume, 0.0) / advMinute : 0.0
rangeAtr = nz(atrSes, 0.0) > 0 ? (high - low) / atrSes : 0.0

// Measured to the bar's extremes, not its close, so the value can only grow as
// the minute develops. That is what keeps a live marker from disappearing.
refPx  = nz(close[impulseLen], close)
upExc  = high - refPx
dnExc  = refPx - low
isUp   = upExc >= dnExc
excPct = refPx > 0 ? 100.0 * math.max(upExc, dnExc) / refPx : 0.0

// Conviction 0-100. Ratio-to-threshold on each active gate, capped at 3x, so
// meeting every threshold exactly lands near 50 and doubling them lands at 100.
// It ranks signals; it never creates them.
// The inputs, used directly. No preset, no override.
eRvol  = minRvol
eAdv   = minAdvRatio
eRng   = minRangeAtr
eMove  = minMovePct
eAbsOn = useAbsGate

// Second route in, for reactions that arrive as a staircase rather than one
// violent candle. Both terms are monotonic inside a live bar, like the rest.
vol3   = nz(volume, 0) + nz(volume[1], 0) + nz(volume[2], 0)
ref3   = nz(close[3], close)
hi3    = math.max(high, nz(high[1], high), nz(high[2], high))
lo3    = math.min(low, nz(low[1], low), nz(low[2], low))
move3  = ref3 > 0 ? 100.0 * math.max(hi3 - ref3, ref3 - lo3) / ref3 : 0.0
burst3 = advMinute > 0 ? vol3 / (3.0 * advMinute) : 0.0

c1 = eRvol > 0 ? math.min(rvol     / eRvol, 3.0) : 1.0
c2 = eRng  > 0 ? math.min(rangeAtr / eRng,  3.0) : 1.0
c3 = eMove > 0 ? math.min(excPct   / eMove, 3.0) : 1.0
float c4 = eAbsOn and eAdv > 0 ? math.min(advRatio / eAdv, 3.0) : na
cN = na(c4) ? (c1 + c2 + c3) / 3.0 : (c1 + c2 + c3 + c4) / 4.0
score = math.round(math.min(100.0, 100.0 * cN / 2.0))


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// FILTERS AND SIGNAL
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

inSess = sessMode == "Post-market only" ? inPost :
     sessMode == "Pre-market only" ? inPre : (inPre or inPost)

minOfDay   = hour * 60 + minute
preOpenOk  = preOpenGuard <= 0 or not inPre or minOfDay < (570 - preOpenGuard)
guardOk    = bucketBars >= guardBars
armed      = bucket >= 0 and not na(medVol) and not na(atrSes) and medVol > 0 and atrSes > 0

// The "once only" allowance is keyed on the session block (sessStartMs uniquely
// identifies this pre-market or this post-market), never on the calendar day -
// see the input tooltip for the COHR case that forced this.
var int lastFireBar = na
var int lastFireBlock = na
coolOk = na(lastFireBar) or (bar_index - lastFireBar) >= cooldownBars
dayOk  = not oneShot or na(lastFireBlock) or lastFireBlock != sessStartMs

volOk = rvol     >= eRvol
rngOk = rangeAtr >= eRng
movOk = excPct   >= eMove
absOk = not eAbsOn or eAdv <= 0 or advMinute <= 0 or advRatio >= eAdv

burstOk = useBurst and volOk and burst3 >= minBurstVol and move3 >= minBurstMove

// Chart-native absolute-size gate. Passes automatically until enough regular
// hours bars exist to form a median, so a fresh chart is never dead.
rthOk = not useRthGate or na(rthMed) or rthMed <= 0 or rthRatio >= minRthMult

gatesOk = ((volOk and rngOk and movOk and absOk) or burstOk) and rthOk

// Escalation gate: after a signal, the next one must either flip direction or
// beat the last on BOTH volume and move. Never caps the session - a genuinely
// bigger or opposite event always gets through.
thisDir = isUp ? 1 : -1
escBase = not useEscalate or lastSigDir == 0 or thisDir != lastSigDir or
     (nz(volume, 0) > nz(lastSigVol, 0) and excPct > nz(lastSigExc, 0))

// A second print in the SAME direction while a trade is already open tells you
// nothing you are not already acting on - it just clutters the chart with a
// duplicate stop and target set. This is the SPCE case: the second signal was
// genuinely bigger on both volume and move, so the escalation gate passed it
// correctly, but you were already short and did not need telling twice.
// A FLIP still gets through while a trade is open - that is the reversal
// warning, and it is the one re-fire that matters.
sameDirWhileOpen = suppressWhileOpen and trDir != 0 and thisDir == trDir
escOk = escBase and not sameDirWhileOpen

raw     = armed and inSess and guardOk and preOpenOk and gatesOk
trigger = raw and coolOk and dayOk and escOk and (liveMode or barstate.isconfirmed)


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// RENDER
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

f_num(x, p) => str.tostring(x, p)

if trigger
    lastFireBar := bar_index
    lastFireBlock := sessStartMs
    lastSigDir := thisDir
    lastSigVol := volume
    lastSigExc := excPct

    col = isUp ? colUp : colDn

    tip = "EARNINGS PRINT  " + (isUp ? "UP" : "DOWN") + "\n" +
     syminfo.ticker + "  " + str.tostring(close, format.mintick) + "\n" +
     "+" + str.tostring(intoMin) + " min into " + (inPre ? "pre-market" : "post-market") + "\n" +
     "-----------------------\n" +
     (burstOk and not rngOk ? "triggered by the 3-BAR BURST route\n" : "") +
     "RVOL          " + f_num(rvol, "#.#")     + "x   (need " + f_num(eRvol, "#.#") + ")\n" +
     "Range / ATR   " + f_num(rangeAtr, "#.#")  + "x   (need " + f_num(eRng, "#.#")  + ")\n" +
     "Excursion     " + f_num(excPct, "#.##")   + "%   (need " + f_num(eMove, "#.##") + ")\n" +
     "vs RTH minute " + f_num(advRatio, "#.##") + "x" + (eAbsOn ? "   (need " + f_num(eAdv, "#.##") + ")" : "   (gate off)") + "\n" +
     "3-bar burst   " + f_num(burst3, "#.##") + "x vol, " + f_num(move3, "#.##") + "% move\n" +
     "-----------------------\n" +
     "Conviction    " + str.tostring(score) + " / 100"

    label.new(
     bar_index, isUp ? low : high,
     isUp ? "▲" : "▼",
     yloc      = isUp ? yloc.belowbar : yloc.abovebar,
     style     = isUp ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down,
     color     = col,
     textcolor = color.white,
     size      = size.normal,
     tooltip   = tip)

    if showLevels
        float ext  = isUp ? high : low
        float f50  = ext + (refPx - ext) * 0.5
        float f618 = ext + (refPx - ext) * 0.618
        line.new(bar_index, f50,  bar_index + levelLen, f50,  color=color.new(col, 40), style=line.style_dashed, width=1)
        line.new(bar_index, f618, bar_index + levelLen, f618, color=color.new(col, 65), style=line.style_dotted, width=1)

    alert(
     "EARNINGS PRINT " + (isUp ? "UP" : "DOWN") + " - " + syminfo.ticker +
     " @ " + str.tostring(close, format.mintick) +
     " | RVOL " + f_num(rvol, "#.#") + "x" +
     " | range " + f_num(rangeAtr, "#.#") + "x ATR" +
     " | move " + f_num(excPct, "#.##") + "%" +
     " | +" + str.tostring(intoMin) + "m into session" +
     " | conviction " + str.tostring(score) + "/100",
     alert.freq_once_per_bar)

alertcondition(trigger, "Earnings print detected", "Earnings print detected on {{ticker}} at {{close}}")

// v1.9: the duplicate plotshape arrows are gone. Every signal was drawing twice -
// once as a plotshape triangle and once as the label above it.
//
// The label is kept as the single marker rather than the plotshape, because the
// label is what carries the hover tooltip and what can be coloured per element.
// The garbage-collection worry that motivated plotshape in v1.7 turned out to be
// unfounded: measured across the full loaded history, this fires 4-6 times per
// symbol, against a 500-label cap. Two orders of magnitude of headroom.


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// PER-BAR DIAGNOSTICS
//
// The status panel only ever describes the LAST bar, which is useless when the
// question is "why was there no arrow on THAT candle 20 minutes ago". These plot
// into the Data Window (Alt+D on the chart) - hover any historical bar and read
// the exact numbers the gates saw on it, against the thresholds in force.
//
// display.data_window keeps them out of the chart pane and off the price scale.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

plot(rvol,       "· RVOL",            display=display.data_window)
plot(eRvol,      "· RVOL needed",     display=display.data_window)
plot(rangeAtr,   "· Range/ATR",       display=display.data_window)
plot(eRng,       "· Range/ATR needed", display=display.data_window)
plot(excPct,     "· Excursion %",     display=display.data_window)
plot(eMove,      "· Excursion needed", display=display.data_window)
plot(advRatio,   "· vs RTH minute",   display=display.data_window)
plot(eAdv,       "· vs RTH needed",   display=display.data_window)
plot(burst3,     "· 3bar vol x",      display=display.data_window)
plot(move3,      "· 3bar move %",     display=display.data_window)
plot(armed   ? 1 : 0, "· armed (1=yes)",     display=display.data_window)
plot(gatesOk ? 1 : 0, "· gates pass (1=yes)", display=display.data_window)
plot(trigger ? 1 : 0, "· FIRED (1=yes)",      display=display.data_window)
plot(bucket,     "· bucket 0-3",      display=display.data_window)
plot(baseN,      "· baseline samples", display=display.data_window)


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// CONTINUATION CONFIRM
//
// The print marker says "the release just hit". It does NOT say "this move
// continues" - measured across [n] prints, the print candle's extreme was taken
// out [n]% of the time, but the session still tended to close BELOW that extreme.
// The move overshoots, extends a bit further, then hands much of it back.
//
// So this second marker fires only when the move has proven two things at a bar
// CLOSE: it made a new extreme beyond the print candle, and it is still holding
// most of the impulse. That pair measured [n]% win / [n]R where entering
// immediately measured [n]% / [n]R.
//
// Evaluated on confirmed bars only - deliberately unlike the print marker. The
// giveback test uses the close, which can move both ways inside a bar, so a live
// version would flicker and would not match what was backtested.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

var int   impBar = na
var float impA   = na
var float impE   = na
var int   impDir = 0
var bool  impDone = false
var bool  invFired = false
var float impOpp = na       // print candle's OPPOSITE extreme - the real stop anchor

// Plain (non-var) flags so the confirm marker can also be a plotshape rather than
// a garbage-collectable label. Reset to false every bar, set true on the bar that
// confirms.
bool confirmNow = false
bool confirmUp  = false

// ─── LIVE TRADE STATE, opened by a confirm ─────────────────────────────────────
// Exit rules compared on [n] confirmed signals before this state was written:
//
//     flat stop, 1R target ................ [n]R
//     flat stop, 2R target ................ [n]R
//     breakeven at +0.5R, 1R target ....... [n]R
//     scale half at [n]R, rest to 1R ..... [n]R
//     scale half at [n]R, rest to 2R ..... [n]R
// Later versions removed this table because it came from a different data feed
// than TradingView bars.
var float trEntry  = na
var float trStop   = na
var float trTarget = na          // TP1, 1R
var float trTarget2 = na         // TP2, 2R
var float trTarget3 = na         // TP3, 3R
var int   trBar    = na
var bool  trTp1Done = false
var bool  trTp2Done = false
var line  lnStop = na
var line  lnTp1  = na
var line  lnTp2  = na
var line  lnTp3  = na
var int   lnSess = na       // session block the current level set belongs to

if trigger
    impBar  := bar_index
    impA    := nz(close[1], close)
    impE    := isUp ? high : low
    impDir  := isUp ? 1 : -1
    impDone := false
    impOpp  := isUp ? low : high
    // DISARM invalidation on a new print. It re-arms only when that print earns
    // a confirm. Resetting it to false here was the bug that let an "!" fire off
    // the PREVIOUS trade's state before the new one had confirmed anything.
    invFired := true

if showConfirm and barstate.isconfirmed and not impDone and not na(impBar) and impDir != 0
    if bar_index > impBar and (bar_index - impBar) <= confirmWindow
        float impR = math.abs(impE - impA)
        bool  newExt = impDir > 0 ? high > impE : low < impE
        float favE = (impE - impA) * impDir
        float favC = (close - impA) * impDir
        float give = impR > 0 ? (favE - favC) / impR : 1.0
        // Where this bar closes inside its own range, in the trade's direction.
        // A poke to a new extreme that closes back down is a rejection.
        float cbRng = math.max(high - low, syminfo.mintick)
        float cbLoc = impDir > 0 ? (close - low) / cbRng : (high - close) / cbRng
        bool  closeOk = minConfClose <= 0.0 or cbLoc >= minConfClose
        if impR > 0 and newExt and closeOk and give < maxGiveback / 100.0
            impDone := true
            confirmNow := true
            confirmUp := impDir > 0
            // STOP ANCHOR - the PRINT candle's opposite extreme, not this bar's.
            // The confirm bar's own extreme is a [n]%-of-price stop on a name
            // that just moved 6%; it gets taken out by noise within a minute or
            // two, which closes the trade before any target can be reached. That
            // is exactly why no take-profit marker ever appeared on a clean
            // trend. Anchoring to the print candle gives a [n]% stop, which is
            // also the placement that measured best ([n]R at a 3R target vs
            // [n]R for the tight one).
            // Stop sits a FRACTION of the way from entry back toward the print
            // candle's far side. 1.0 = the far side itself (v2.7, too wide -
            // a full round trip on a 6% earnings move). 0.5 measured identically
            // on win rate and R-expectancy while halving the cash at risk:
            //     0.35 -> [n]% win, [n]R, stop [n]% of price   (too tight)
            //     0.50 -> [n]% win, [n]R, stop [n]% of price   <- shipped
            //     1.00 -> [n]% win, [n]R, stop [n]% of price
            float farPx  = na(impOpp) ? (impDir > 0 ? low : high) : impOpp
            float stopPx = close + stopRetrace * (farPx - close)
            float riskPx = math.abs(close - stopPx)
            float tgtPx  = close + riskPx * impDir
            if riskPx > 0
                trDir     := impDir
                trEntry   := close
                trStop    := stopPx
                trTarget  := close + riskPx * 1.0 * impDir
                trTarget2 := close + riskPx * 2.0 * impDir
                trTarget3 := close + riskPx * 3.0 * impDir
                trBar     := bar_index
                trTp1Done := false
                trTp2Done := false
                invFired  := false     // re-arm: this trade may now be invalidated
                // Previous trade's lines are left exactly as they are: still
                // extending right, forever. Two earlier attempts at being clever
                // here were both wrong - deleting them lost the older trade's
                // stop entirely, and freezing them at the exit bar produced the
                // short staggered stubs. Every level stays full width.
                if showTradeLines
                    // extend.none + an x2 that is pushed forward every bar of the
                    // SAME session. The levels therefore span the whole extended
                    // session they belong to and stop at its end, instead of
                    // running across the following days.
                    lnSess := sessStartMs
                    lnStop := line.new(bar_index, stopPx, bar_index + 1, stopPx,
                     color=colStop2, style=line.style_dashed, width=2)
                    lnTp1 := line.new(bar_index, trTarget, bar_index + 1, trTarget,
                     color=colTp, style=line.style_dotted, width=1)
                    lnTp2 := line.new(bar_index, trTarget2, bar_index + 1, trTarget2,
                     color=colTp, style=line.style_dotted, width=1)
                    lnTp3 := line.new(bar_index, trTarget3, bar_index + 1, trTarget3,
                     color=color.new(colTp, 45), style=line.style_dotted, width=1)
            label.new(
             bar_index, impDir > 0 ? high : low,
             "✓",
             yloc      = impDir > 0 ? yloc.abovebar : yloc.belowbar,
             style     = impDir > 0 ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up,
             color     = colConf,
             textcolor = impDir > 0 ? colUp : colDn,
             size      = size.small,
             tooltip   = "CONTINUATION CONFIRMED  " + (impDir > 0 ? "LONG" : "SHORT") + "\n" +
             syminfo.ticker + "\n" +
             "-----------------------\n" +
             "new extreme beyond the print bar: yes\n" +
             "impulse retained: " + str.tostring(100.0 * (1.0 - give), "#.#") + "%\n" +
             "-----------------------\n" +
             "entry (this close)  " + str.tostring(close, format.mintick) + "\n" +
             "structural stop     " + str.tostring(stopPx, format.mintick) + "\n" +
             "1R target           " + str.tostring(tgtPx, format.mintick) + "\n" +
             "risk                " + str.tostring(100.0 * riskPx / close, "#.##") + "% of price\n" +
             "-----------------------\n" +
             "Base rate for this setup: [n]% win, [n]R (n=[n]).\n" +
             "Small sample.")
            alert("CONTINUATION CONFIRMED " + (impDir > 0 ? "LONG" : "SHORT") + " - " + syminfo.ticker +
             " @ " + str.tostring(close, format.mintick) +
             " | stop " + str.tostring(stopPx, format.mintick) +
             " | 1R target " + str.tostring(tgtPx, format.mintick) +
             " | risk " + str.tostring(100.0 * riskPx / close, "#.##") + "%",
             alert.freq_once_per_bar)
    else if (bar_index - impBar) > confirmWindow
        impDone := true


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// LIVE DIAGNOSTICS PANEL
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

f_pos() =>
    tblPos == "Top left"      ? position.top_left :
     tblPos == "Bottom right" ? position.bottom_right :
     tblPos == "Bottom left"  ? position.bottom_left :
     tblPos == "Middle right" ? position.middle_right : position.top_right

var table diag = table.new(f_pos(), 3, 10, border_width=1, frame_width=1,
     frame_color=color.new(color.gray, 60), border_color=color.new(color.gray, 75))

f_row(int r, string k, float v, string vf, float need, bool ok, bool active) =>
    table.cell(diag, 0, r, k, text_color=color.new(color.white, active ? 30 : 70), text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=color.new(color.black, 82))
    table.cell(diag, 1, r, f_num(v, vf), text_color=not active ? color.new(color.gray, 50) : ok ? color.new(#00e676, 0) : color.new(color.white, 25), text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_right, bgcolor=color.new(color.black, 82))
    table.cell(diag, 2, r, active ? f_num(need, vf) : "off", text_color=color.new(color.gray, 20), text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_right, bgcolor=color.new(color.black, 82))

if showTable and barstate.islast
    status = not armed    ? "BUILDING BASELINE" :
     not inSess           ? "OUT OF SESSION" :
     not guardOk          ? "SESSION GUARD" :
     not preOpenOk        ? "PRE-OPEN EXCLUDED" :
     gatesOk and coolOk and dayOk ? "★ PRINT DETECTED" :
     gatesOk and not dayOk ? "ALREADY FIRED THIS SESSION" :
     gatesOk and not coolOk ? "COOLDOWN" : "ARMED"

    statusCol = status == "★ PRINT DETECTED" ? (isUp ? colUp : colDn) :
     status == "ARMED" ? color.new(#2962ff, 0) : color.new(color.gray, 25)

    hdr = "EPD " + VERSION + "  " + (bucket < 0 ? "-" : (inPre ? "pre" : "post") + " +" + str.tostring(intoMin) + "m")
    table.cell(diag, 0, 0, hdr, text_color=color.new(color.white, 0), text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=color.new(color.black, 70))
    table.cell(diag, 1, 0, "now",  text_color=color.new(color.gray, 20), text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_right, bgcolor=color.new(color.black, 70))
    table.cell(diag, 2, 0, "need", text_color=color.new(color.gray, 20), text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_right, bgcolor=color.new(color.black, 70))

    f_row(1, "RVOL",        rvol,     "#.#",  eRvol, volOk, true)
    f_row(2, "Range / ATR", rangeAtr, "#.#",  eRng,  rngOk, true)
    f_row(3, "Excursion %", excPct,   "#.##", eMove, movOk, true)
    f_row(4, "vs RTH med",  rthRatio, "#.##", minRthMult, rthOk, useRthGate)

    table.cell(diag, 0, 5, "Conviction", text_color=color.new(color.white, 30), text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=color.new(color.black, 82))
    table.cell(diag, 1, 5, str.tostring(score), text_color=color.new(color.white, 0), text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_right, bgcolor=color.new(color.black, 82))
    table.cell(diag, 2, 5, "/100", text_color=color.new(color.gray, 20), text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_right, bgcolor=color.new(color.black, 82))

    table.cell(diag, 0, 6, status, text_color=color.white, text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=color.new(statusCol, 55))
    table.cell(diag, 1, 6, "", bgcolor=color.new(statusCol, 55))
    table.cell(diag, 2, 6, "", bgcolor=color.new(statusCol, 55))

    // ── live trade + measured odds ─────────────────────────────────────────────
    trTxt = trDir == 0 ? "no open setup" : (trDir > 0 ? "LONG from " : "SHORT from ") + str.tostring(trEntry, format.mintick)
    trCol = trDir == 0 ? color.new(color.gray, 25) : (trDir > 0 ? colUp : colDn)
    float trR = trDir != 0 and not na(trEntry) and not na(trStop) and math.abs(trEntry - trStop) > 0 ?
     ((close - trEntry) * trDir) / math.abs(trEntry - trStop) : na
    table.cell(diag, 0, 7, trTxt, text_color=color.white, text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=color.new(trCol, 70))
    table.cell(diag, 1, 7, na(trR) ? "-" : f_num(trR, "#.##") + "R", text_color=color.white, text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_right, bgcolor=color.new(trCol, 70))
    table.cell(diag, 2, 7, trDir == 0 ? "" : "now", text_color=color.new(color.gray, 20), text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_right, bgcolor=color.new(trCol, 70))

    table.cell(diag, 0, 8, "stop / target", text_color=color.new(color.white, 30), text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=color.new(color.black, 82))
    table.cell(diag, 1, 8, trDir == 0 ? "-" : str.tostring(trStop, format.mintick), text_color=color.new(#ff8a80, 0), text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_right, bgcolor=color.new(color.black, 82))
    table.cell(diag, 2, 8, trDir == 0 ? "-" : str.tostring(trTarget, format.mintick), text_color=color.new(#b9f6ca, 0), text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_right, bgcolor=color.new(color.black, 82))

    // Base rates measured on [n] confirmed signals, [n] earnings events.
    table.cell(diag, 0, 9, "odds  [n]R / [n]R", text_color=color.new(color.white, 30), text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=color.new(color.black, 82))
    table.cell(diag, 1, 9, "[n]%", text_color=color.new(color.white, 10), text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_right, bgcolor=color.new(color.black, 82))
    table.cell(diag, 2, 9, "[n]%", text_color=color.new(color.white, 10), text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_right, bgcolor=color.new(color.black, 82))


// v1.9: confirm plotshapes removed too - same duplicate-marker problem. The
// confirm is now a single label whose badge stays yellow but whose TICK is
// coloured by the direction of the print it belongs to: green tick = bullish
// continuation, red tick = bearish. See the label.new call above.


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// EXIT MARKERS
//
// A confirm opens a tracked trade. Two things can end it, and each prints once:
//
//   $  TARGET - price reached [n]R. Measured: [n]% of confirmed signals get here
//                before the stop, and a flat 1R target is the tracked exit.
//   ✕  STOP - price hit the confirm bar's opposite extreme.
//
// [n]% of confirmed trades do eventually give the entire earnings move back - but in every one
// of those, the structural stop had ALREADY triggered at or before the move was fully erased. A
// separate "whole move lost" marker would never tell you anything the ✕ had not already said
// several minutes earlier. It is available below as `showInvalidation`, default OFF, so you can
// see that on the chart.
//
// Evaluated live rather than on bar close: these are price levels, and a touch
// is a touch. High only rises and low only falls inside a bar, so neither marker
// can appear and then vanish.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

bool tp1Now  = false
bool tp2Now  = false
bool stopNow = false
bool invNow  = false
int  exitDir = 0        // captured BEFORE trDir is cleared, or the marker lands wrong

bool tp3Now = false

if trDir != 0 and not na(trBar) and bar_index > trBar
    // Stop is checked FIRST. Within a single bar we cannot know which level was
    // touched first, so assume the unfavourable one - never book a target the
    // bar might not have reached before stopping out.
    bool stHit = trDir > 0 ? low <= trStop : high >= trStop
    bool t1Hit = trDir > 0 ? high >= trTarget : low <= trTarget
    bool t2Hit = trDir > 0 ? high >= trTarget2 : low <= trTarget2
    bool t3Hit = trDir > 0 ? high >= trTarget3 : low <= trTarget3
    if stHit
        stopNow := true
        exitDir := trDir
        trDir := 0
    else
        if t1Hit and not trTp1Done
            tp1Now := true
            trTp1Done := true
        if t2Hit and not trTp2Done
            tp2Now := true
            trTp2Done := true
        if t3Hit
            tp3Now := true
            exitDir := trDir
            trDir := 0

// Push the levels forward for every bar of the session they were drawn in -
// whether or not the trade is still open. They stop growing automatically when
// the session block changes, so each set of levels spans exactly its own
// extended-hours session and never bleeds into the next day.
if showTradeLines and not na(lnSess) and lnSess == sessStartMs and bucket >= 0
    if not na(lnStop)
        line.set_x2(lnStop, bar_index)
    if not na(lnTp1)
        line.set_x2(lnTp1, bar_index)
    if not na(lnTp2)
        line.set_x2(lnTp2, bar_index)
    if not na(lnTp3)
        line.set_x2(lnTp3, bar_index)

// Full invalidation - ONLY after a confirm, never after a bare print.
// The old version was gated on impBar (the print candle), so it fired on prints
// that never produced a confirm at all. That is why an "!" appeared before any
// yellow tick. Every exit marker in this script belongs to a CONFIRMED trade, so
// this one is gated on trBar like the rest.
if showInvalidation and not na(trBar) and bar_index > trBar and not na(impA) and not invFired
    int invDir = trDir != 0 ? trDir : exitDir
    if invDir != 0
        bool back = invDir > 0 ? low <= impA : high >= impA
        if back
            invNow := true
            invFired := true

if tp1Now
    label.new(bar_index, trDir > 0 or exitDir > 0 ? low : high, "T1",
     yloc = (trDir > 0 or exitDir > 0) ? yloc.belowbar : yloc.abovebar,
     style = (trDir > 0 or exitDir > 0) ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down,
     color = colTp, textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny,
     tooltip = "TP1 — +1R reached\nentry " + str.tostring(trEntry, format.mintick) +
     "  TP1 " + str.tostring(trTarget, format.mintick) +
     "\n\nThe share of confirmed signals that reach this level is redacted.")

if tp2Now
    label.new(bar_index, (trDir > 0 or exitDir > 0) ? low : high, "T2",
     yloc = (trDir > 0 or exitDir > 0) ? yloc.belowbar : yloc.abovebar,
     style = (trDir > 0 or exitDir > 0) ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down,
     color = colTp, textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny,
     tooltip = "TP2 — +2R reached\nentry " + str.tostring(trEntry, format.mintick) +
     "  TP2 " + str.tostring(trTarget2, format.mintick))

if tp3Now
    label.new(bar_index, exitDir > 0 ? low : high, "T3",
     yloc = exitDir > 0 ? yloc.belowbar : yloc.abovebar,
     style = exitDir > 0 ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down,
     color = colTp, textcolor = color.white, size = size.small,
     tooltip = "TP3 — [n]R reached, trade closed\nentry " + str.tostring(trEntry, format.mintick) +
     "  TP3 " + str.tostring(trTarget3, format.mintick))

if stopNow
    label.new(bar_index, high, "✕",
     yloc = yloc.abovebar, style = label.style_label_down,
     color = colStop, textcolor = color.white, size = size.small,
     tooltip = "STOP hit\nentry " + str.tostring(trEntry, format.mintick) +
     "  stop " + str.tostring(trStop, format.mintick) +
     "\n\nThis is the trade being wrong. The share of confirmed signals that end here is redacted.")

if invNow
    label.new(bar_index, high, "!",
     yloc = yloc.abovebar, style = label.style_label_down,
     color = color.new(#9e9e9e, 20), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny,
     tooltip = "Entire earnings move given back.\nMeasured: the structural stop fired at or before this point in [n] of [n] cases, so this marker is informational only.")

// Last-resort visibility check. If this is ever ON and you still see no arrow,
// the problem is drawing, not detection.
plot(confirmNow ? 1 : 0, "· CONFIRMED (1=yes)", display=display.data_window)


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// DEBUG OVERLAY - off by default. See the input tooltip for how to read it.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
plotshape(debugSess and bucket >= 0, "· debug: extended-hours bar", style=shape.circle,
     location=location.bottom, color=color.new(#2962ff, 30), size=size.tiny)
plotshape(debugSess and armed, "· debug: armed", style=shape.circle,
     location=location.top, color=color.new(#00e676, 30), size=size.tiny)





